---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    actor Steward
    participant Modal as KmlImportModal<br/>/admin/sites
    participant Bucket as Supabase Storage<br/>bucket kml-imports
    participant Loader as Import server action<br/>importProtectedAreasFromStorage<br/>(utils/kml-import-actions.ts)
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>protected_areas
    participant Pages as Map and admin pages
    participant Geo as /api/geocode route<br/>(no auth check today)
    participant OC as OpenCage API

    Note over Admin,OC: Covers US 6.0.1. The KML/KMZ import exists (#152). The Admin uploads the SAPAA-Map .kml/.kmz export.<br/>sites_pa has no geometry columns. The boundaries are in protected_areas, keyed by UNIQUE (folder, fid).<br/>"(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.

    Admin->>Modal: Select "Upload Site Data". Choose the SAPAA-Map .kml/.kmz export
    Modal->>Modal: Check the file type and the size (50 MB or less)
    Modal->>Bucket: Upload with the browser Supabase client<br/>to kml-imports/<uploadId>/<file>
    Note right of Bucket: Storage RLS allows insert, select and delete only when<br/>auth.jwt() app_metadata has role = admin and authenticated = true.
    alt Upload refused or fails
        Bucket-->>Modal: Error
        Modal-->>Admin: Show "The upload failed"
    else Upload done
        Bucket-->>Modal: OK
        Modal->>Loader: importProtectedAreasFromStorage(storagePath)
        activate Loader
        Loader->>Loader: isApprovedAdmin() reads app_metadata.role<br/>and app_metadata.authenticated from auth.getUser()
        alt Caller is not Admin
            Loader-->>Modal: { success: false, error: "Only admins can import protected areas." }
        else Path does not match IMPORT_PATH_PATTERN
            Loader-->>Modal: { success: false, error: "The import path is not valid." }
        else Caller is Admin and the path is valid
            Loader->>Bucket: Download the staged file with the service role
            Bucket-->>Loader: File bytes
            Loader->>Loader: parseProtectedAreaFile (lib/map/kmlImport.ts).<br/>fid = -1 (NO_FID) when a placemark has no FID
            loop Each chunk of 50 rows
                Loader->>DB: Upsert into protected_areas, onConflict folder,fid:<br/>folder, fid, name, area_type, oc_name, geometry (MultiPolygon jsonb),<br/>date_res, area_ha, updated_at
            end
            Loader->>Bucket: In a finally block: remove the staged file, then sweepStaleUploads
            Loader-->>Modal: Report upserted and skipped counts and warnings
        end
        deactivate Loader
        Modal-->>Admin: Show the result or the error
    end

    %% Not merged. protected_areas.site_id was dropped in 20261006010000, so the match needs a new link column.
    opt Match each active site to a boundary (proposed, AT 1 to AT 3)
        Loader->>DB: Read active sites_pa rows (proposed)
        DB-->>Loader: Active sites
        loop Each active site
            Loader->>Loader: Match site name to a protected_areas row (proposed)
            alt Match is found
                Loader->>DB: Store the link in a new link column (proposed, AT 1, AT 2)
            else No match
                Loader->>Loader: Leave the site with no link (proposed, AT 3)
            end
        end
    end
    opt Open unmatched sites list (proposed)
        Admin->>Pages: Open unmatched sites list (proposed)
        Pages->>DB: Read active sites_pa rows with no link (proposed)
        DB-->>Pages: Unmatched sites (the AT 3 list)
        Pages-->>Admin: Show sites for an Admin to fix
    end

    opt A site has no point and fallback geocoding is used (AT 4)
        Pages->>Geo: GET /api/geocode?q=site name (exists. Today the only caller is<br/>admin/dashboard/page.tsx, which geocodes every site by name in a loop)
        Geo->>Geo: Look for a cached result for this name (proposed)
        alt Cached result exists
            Geo-->>Pages: lat, lng from the cache. No OpenCage request
        else No cached result
            Geo->>Geo: Read the OpenCage request count for today (proposed)
            alt Count has reached the daily limit of 2,500
                Geo-->>Pages: No result. No OpenCage request
            else Count is less than the limit
                Geo->>OC: Geocode request. Add 1 to the count for today (proposed)
                alt External API returns a result
                    OC-->>Geo: lat, lng
                    Geo->>Geo: Store the result in the cache (proposed)
                    Geo-->>Pages: { latitude, longitude }
                else External API refuses the request or its quota is exhausted
                    OC-->>Geo: Error or no result
                    Geo-->>Pages: { coords: null }
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Steward->>Pages: Open the map (proposed)
    Pages->>DB: Read protected_areas.geometry (proposed). No centre point column now
    DB-->>Pages: Geometry
    Pages-->>Steward: Draw site on the map

    Note over Pages,OC: Open question: where the geocode cache and the daily request count are stored,<br/>for example a database table or server memory. The proposed ER diagram does not show them yet.<br/>StewardLog calls OpenCage separately from the phone. If it uses the same key, its requests also count.
